{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it","id":991833,"title":"Space 2, does anyone do without it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-23T06:58:25-07:00","id":991833,"title":"Space 2, does anyone do without it?","content":"This post may be odd, but I have noticed that pretty much every player character in our games either starts with, or rapidly acquires Space at 2 dots. They may almost never use it aside from its sympathetic range attainment and scrying, but every player (including me) feels that this ability is de rigueur for any serious mage. Any arcanum is of incredible use, but this one has gotten the reputation for being indispensable. For what I can only call aesthetic reasons, it bugs me to see this arcanum so favored (even though I admit my characters snap it up as well).<br /> <br /> My question is, do other players find this typical in their games? Each of our players is constantly finding themselves in a situation wherein that particular skill set is needed - how many players don't use space and don't particularly feel crippled by the lack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T07:06:56-07:00","id":991836,"title":"","content":"Few are the characters that I've seen that don't start with Space 2 or attempt to acquire it in short order. The ability to extend your cast range infinitely (if with some restrictions) is a pretty potent thing. I mean, you could make do without it, sure, <i>but why would you</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T07:40:59-07:00","id":991847,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's really no compelling reason not to take Space 2 ASAP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T07:45:29-07:00","id":991849,"title":"","content":"All my characters used to have Space 2 because I like the esoteric (by our standards) Arcana. I also fancied myself a Jedi knight, so I kind of needed scrying and omnivision and stuff like that. Then I tried to make characters without it and that's how I discovered the awesomeness of other Arcana.<br /> <br /> When everybody is using Space magic to do something, it makes it really easy for rivals and enemies to take advantage or counter that. Diversifying your magical skill set is the best way to explore magic and get the upper hand on your enemies.<br /> <br /> I've discovered that my new go-to Arcanum has become Forces. Even my favorite Acanthus character had Time 3, Fate 3, Forces 2, Spirit 1 and I was so happy. No need for Space at all. That's what the Oathbreakers are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T07:59:31-07:00","id":991853,"title":"","content":"Isn't Prime similarly must-have? If you're not playing a Magistos or Obrimos you kind of need to pick one or the other, at least initially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T08:18:23-07:00","id":991858,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I personally tend to rush Prime myself, but Space is sexy and cool too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T08:46:42-07:00","id":991861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=991853#post991853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Prime similarly must-have? If you're not playing a Magistos or Obrimos you kind of need to pick one or the other, at least initially.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only mages we have that use prime have it as one of their primary Arcana, and the others get by fine for the most part. In fact, all the mages in our games only take Arcana they plan to use as primary Arcana. They tend to have three to four Arcana, all of which they use and improve comparably - they may specialize a bit in one or the other of their major Arcana, but for the most part all the Arcana they have are major parts of their role as a mage. Except space. Only one mage has ever used space as one of his primary tools, but every single one has space 2. If there was any other arcana this happens to, it wouldn't bother me, but as it is I feel as if something is off.<br /> But apparently it is not unusual ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 10-23-2016, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T09:48:21-07:00","id":991880,"title":"","content":"I don't think I've ever played in a game where everyone takes Space 2. Typically we let the Mastigos do Space, and deal with it as an interesting limitation if the Mastigos doesn't happen to be available for the current session. I've had games where other people take Space, but that was typically worked into specific plans they had (like the Acanthus who wanted to be able to integrate Space into his postcognitions and divinations).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:39:27-07:00","id":991954,"title":"","content":"It feels somewhat less necessary than it did in 1st edition, mostly because there's so much more you can do without risking Paradox now, but it's still <i>pretty</i> necessary. The fact that Counterspell Prime isn't a spell anymore means you don't take it as a Rote like you used to basically have to <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Space is just a flat-out awesome, though, so really you should end up taking it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:07:02-07:00","id":991974,"title":"","content":"What do you see them using it for? Just casting beyond sensory range? Does it come up that much?<br /> <br /> I suppose the advantage I could see is being able to cast from a demesne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-23-2016, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:02:35-07:00","id":992439,"title":"","content":"Well, I do have to say that I personally find it cool that the reason that mages take shadow names is because of my favorite arcanum. However, there's a not insignificant part of me that feels slightly offended that people study that arcanum only for its LESSER attainment. Space has so much more to offer than simply extending your reach! Consider the mage that disappears when walking around corners (obviously teleporting), but yet the security footage doesn't show him finishing the corner from one angle and clearly rounding the corner from the other. How does he do it? Or what about the bachelor pad inside that small apartment that is definitely larger on the inside than the outside? Forget where you put something? Space has the answer (psst, it's right next to you). Want to have five homes, all interconnected? Space has what you need. Need to get past that frustrating security guard keeping you from that grimoire that sleepers think is a first edition copy of Dante's Inferno? Space is the answer. Need to strike five enemies at once but don't want to risk paradox more than is necessary? The ADEPT attainment of Space has your back (at the small price of some mana). Want to hide your sanctum Black family mansion style? The practice of Unmaking of Space is there to help you.<br /> <br /> *Sigh.* It really does feel like it takes a thousand words to paint a picture....hmm something there. Yes, I think I shall call myself Escher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:32:25-07:00","id":992620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=991974#post991974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you see them using it for? Just casting beyond sensory range? Does it come up that much?<br /> <br /> I suppose the advantage I could see is being able to cast from a demesne.</div> </div> </div> </div>They use it for long distance casting and scrying. Yes, it comes up a lot. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:45:13-07:00","id":992623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=992439#post992439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I do have to say that I personally find it cool that the reason that mages take shadow names is because of my favorite arcanum. However, there's a not insignificant part of me that feels slightly offended that people study that arcanum only for its LESSER attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, most of them literally have never used space for anything other than casting beyond sensory range, and scrying. Its not that they couldn't see the uses of Space if they were interested in it, its that they aren't really - they have other things going on. Somehow the concept of being able to use magic on and see distant locations seems intrinsic to the ability to use magic at all, so in their minds (and sometimes mine) those two abilities stand separate from the rest of the Space arcanum as a whole. We considered tweaking the rules so that those two abilities were unattached to a specific arcanum, but couldn't think of anyway to do it without making more changes to the magic system than we wanted to (we've done it before - by the end of 1st ED mage, we were playing under rules with only 7 Arcana, but we didn't want to twist 2nd Ed that much).<br /> <br /> I was mainly interested in whether other players find it difficult to function without the abilities of Space 2, or if we were just looking at thinks wrongly. It seems grabbing Space at 2 is more common than not, but doesn't bother most players like it does me.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T17:03:39-07:00","id":992639,"title":"","content":"If you wanted to hack that I'd suggest something like a Material Sympathetic connection can be Scrutinized with Focused Mage Sight with &quot;Scrying&quot; being Deep Information beneath an Opacity of the target's Withstand rating. From there you could just use the Remote Viewing casting rules. Then you just have to figure out how comfortable you are with how often they need to go through the Scutiny process to access those options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T18:31:03-07:00","id":992667,"title":"","content":"For the one long term Mage game I was in, I was the only character with Space, and none of the other players ever felt I outclassed them (the group managed to max out every Arcana among us by the end of it, except, like, Time and Death). That being said, I went all in on Space and Spirit, so I had kind of an odd combination. I dealt with more issues with Firearms...<br /> <br /> That being said, this was using kinda &quot;1.5&quot; rules (<b>God-Machine</b> + Dave's down and dirty <b>Mage </b>patch).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T19:33:46-07:00","id":992698,"title":"","content":"For the people who always have Space 2 in their groups and games, when running, do NPCs always have it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=992667#post992667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, I went all in on Space and Spirit, so I had kind of an odd combination.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound odd, how and what did you do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T01:20:18-07:00","id":992844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=991974#post991974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you see them using it for? Just casting beyond sensory range? Does it come up that much?<br /> <br /> I suppose the advantage I could see is being able to cast from a demesne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Casting from a demesne really doesn't benefit sympathetic magic all that much - aside from its use as a Yantra, really, or if you're casting on another demesne.<br /> <br /> Casting at sympathetic range is categorically casting outside the Verge/Demesne, and so does not benefit from the Paradox-free environment therein.<br /> <br /> And yes, sympathetic range does come up quite a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T01:24:11-07:00","id":992845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=992844#post992844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, sympathetic range does come up quite a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>A decent amount less now that &quot;remote viewing&quot; is a distinct range modifier with no Arcanum requirement, I'd think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T03:19:40-07:00","id":992870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=992698#post992698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That does sound odd, how and what did you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I ended up doing a lot of remote viewing and searching for sympathetic connections, and a loooooooot of stepping sideways. And this was at a time when the systems for Space seriously did not want you to ever be able to make useful portals, short of Mastery, so I often felt strangely limited...<br /> <br /> I did <i>like </i>the weird combo, though. I specifically chose those because they're almost never what I gravitate to for Arcana when I play a mage. And he ended up being a favourite character of mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T04:53:43-07:00","id":992889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=992844#post992844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Casting from a demesne really doesn't benefit sympathetic magic all that much - aside from its use as a Yantra, really, or if you're casting on another demesne.<br /> <br /> Casting at sympathetic range is categorically casting outside the Verge/Demesne, and so does not benefit from the Paradox-free environment therein.</div> </div> </div> </div>You also don't need to use a Reach to turn a spell from ritual casting to instant, since you can cast at your leisure. So some better yantra bonuses than you might get out of tools, and an extra Reach.<br /> <br /> But aside from distance those seem like the only benefits to casting at range, which is why I'm surprised that it seems like a necessity to most mage players seem to think it's a must have. It's similar to the sniper thing. Does everyone's character have many dots in Firearms and a specialty in Rifles? Because you get the same advantage of distance and safety by shooting people from a thousand feet away rather than within a range they can retaliate from, unless they too are also snipers. Please note I said similar, not identical, as there's obviously much more you can do with the magic of Awakening than a rifle.<br /> <br /> I'm taking it this is not just about casting on enemies?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> Interesting, for some reason when I was thinking about it 'spirit zoos' came to mind, with ample use of ban dividing everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-25-2016, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T07:39:05-07:00","id":992941,"title":"","content":"I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/926706-2e-technical-adepts-fan-made-legacy#post926706\">a Legacy based on Prime/Space</a>, so guilty as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T09:26:37-07:00","id":992978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=991880#post991880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I've ever played in a game where everyone takes Space 2. Typically we let the Mastigos do Space, and deal with it as an interesting limitation if the Mastigos doesn't happen to be available for the current session. I've had games where other people take Space, but that was typically worked into specific plans they had (like the Acanthus who wanted to be able to integrate Space into his postcognitions and divinations).</div> </div> </div> </div>As a followup, I'll note that <i>I'm</i> usually playing the Mastigos in my group, which has a couple of consequences: firstly, I tend to think more about the potential of the Space Arcanum as a whole (and was usually more interested in using it for doing weird things with geometry and vectors, rather than just wards, teleports, portals, and scrying - and was overjoyed when 2e canonized that aspect of Space rather than forcing me to argue with my Storytellers that yes, Space <i>can</i> do things like that); secondly, when I'm <i>not</i> playing Mastigos, being <i>without</i> my usual Ruling Arcana is part of the challenge. I already <i>know</i> a bunch of cool, interesting things I can do with Space, but not having space means I need to figure out cool, interesting things I can do with, say, Prime.<br /> <br /> I still have a hard time keeping my mouth shut when I can see obvious Space-based solutions our Mastigos player for that game is missing, which is a failing of mine. I'm working on it.<br /> <br /> I should ask the people in my groups who don't usually play Mastigos what they think of Space 2. I know only the one of them bothered picking it up as a supplementary Arcanum in our last game, and prpecisely none of them picked a Legacy that made it Ruling (of course, the one who <i>did</i> was the same guy who picked a Legacy that granted Forces so he'd have no Inferior...)<br /> <br /> As an additional note, I've never seen the ability to act remotely via magic as a prerequisite for it really feeling like magic. Most of the time when I think of magic I think of doing weird stuff in the here and now. Scrying itself is an exception, but things like having to meet a witch's eyes for her to cast a hex on you, the enchanter having to talk to you in person where you can hear his voice for him to put you under his spell, or a wizard calling down lightning from the sky to smite his foes... the wizard calling down lightning from the sky to smite his foes while sitting around three towns away from said foes (or worse yet, countries away) feels <i>less</i> like what I'd usually think of when I think of someone doing magic, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T09:53:17-07:00","id":992992,"title":"","content":"An important question to ask: Does the target of a sympathetic ritual spell feel the &quot;build-up&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T10:04:09-07:00","id":992998,"title":"","content":"In answer to the original question, I've only been in one chronicle so far, and it is currently on hold. We're still in the early portion of the game, so players haven't had the chance to branch out much. So, no, no one else has taken any dots of Space yet (I'm playing the mastigos).<br /> <br /> That being said, the storyteller doesn't understand the draw to Space that I have, and he's the person that brought us all together. So I kind of have my work cut out for me. Or in other words, my group could potentially be biased against it (apart from me, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 10-25-2016, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T10:48:30-07:00","id":993014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=992992#post992992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An important question to ask: Does the target of a sympathetic ritual spell feel the &amp;quot;build-up&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't, because until a spell has been cast it's all just a vivid mental construct in a Mage's mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T10:51:53-07:00","id":993015,"title":"","content":"So they can't be counterspelled? There's another bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T11:12:52-07:00","id":993023,"title":"","content":"In order to counterspell you need to use your active mage sight while watching the mage that's doing the casting.<br /> <br /> Just being the target of a spell does not allow for counterspell regardless of how the spell is cast (ritual, instant, sensory, sympathetically). You also don't feel spells while they're being cast unless, as stated above, you watch the caster with your active mage sight. You'd feel in your peripheral mage sight when a spell has taken effect (even if it's cast using sympathetic range) but by then it's too late for counterspell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":".  Slightly better wording. 10-25-2016, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T12:10:07-07:00","id":993034,"title":"","content":"I end up taking it because I play filthy Mastigoi characters. Hasn't been a pick pickup in my campaign, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T12:33:40-07:00","id":993042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=993015#post993015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they can't be counterspelled? There's another bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>For all intents and purposes, no they can't be, you have to be looking with AMS in the right place to notice the Sympathetic link being connected and acted on in the same split second that the spell is occurring.<br /> <br /> This is a good reason to take Space 1 and periodically check your Sympathetic connections, but you could just as easily be nailed by a sensory range spell by a guy reading a newspaper at a cafe down the street, so...good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:24:35-07:00","id":993122,"title":"","content":"Walking around with Ward at least gives you a Clash anytime someone targets you sympathetically. That's something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:37:54-07:00","id":993135,"title":"","content":"Or with Space magic at all. Since it mentions locking a Space into place though I'm not entirely sure it's mobile. Maybe with a Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:45:59-07:00","id":993144,"title":"","content":"That just seems like a difference in natural targeting factors. A spell that freezes motion could easily be used as an aoe spell, but that still requires changing the targeting factors. Similarly, ward is naturally used on things that &quot;don't move&quot; but I don't see a need to reach in order to cast it on something that does move. This seems especially true since True distance according to Space is how close you are sympathetically, not whether you are in motion or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:09:04-07:00","id":993156,"title":"","content":"There are many who thinks casting sympathetically is incredibly useful, but there are some drawbacks I want to list just in case someone is confused by this thread:<br /> The first is the automatic Mana cost.<br /> The second is having to use a sympathetic yantra. This will eat one yantra slot and gives you no extra dice.<br /> The third is that you have to have a sympathetic connection. This means if you want to cast offensively you need to get something that's connected to your enemy, cast Borrow Threads on that object (which eats one of your active spell slots and often requires more than one Reach, making it a Paradox risk for mages who only invest to Space 2 for the sympathetic attainment) in preparation to your spell.<br /> <br /> Space is absolutely one of the most useful Arcana, but casting sympathetically is not as potent or useful for someone with Space 2 compared to someone with Space 4 or 5 who are much better equiped to gain the connections required for the casting and can bolster them to lower Withstand.<br /> <br /> If you instead manage to stalk an enemy you could instead cast via sensory range to gain more potency (due to lower Withstand) and don't have to worry about Ward.<br /> <br /> <br /> The best use of sympathetic range my Mastigos has had was breaking out of a Pylon's hideout together with two prisoners and some sweet magical loot. By preemptively setting up a safe escape location with Borrow Threads I managed to Co-locate that location with the two prison cells, the two loot rooms and our own location. (The Outward and Inward Eye was helpful to see all those locations at the same time so I could include more than one or two of them.) Then I just dragged people and loot through while the Cabal's eloquent Obrimos kept the Seers busy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:13:09-07:00","id":993157,"title":"","content":"Kind of why I'm surprised it's so often picked. Especially with the Mana cost, but I suppose that deserves another thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:38:39-07:00","id":993221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=993014#post993014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't, because until a spell has been cast it's all just a vivid mental construct in a Mage's mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it, though? A Mage who spends Mana during a ritual casting does so before it's cast and loses said Mana if they abort it early. That suggests that <i>something</i> is forming before it hits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:47:08-07:00","id":993225,"title":"","content":"It doesn't necessarily, it could simply be sublimated back into the Fallen, much like a Mage using it for Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> I'm basing my info off of comments from Dave, but hey, it's your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:09:40-07:00","id":993243,"title":"","content":"Got a link to those? They'd probably help clarify it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:20:29-07:00","id":993246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=993221#post993221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it, though? A Mage who spends Mana during a ritual casting does so before it's cast and loses said Mana if they abort it early. That suggests that <i>something</i> is forming before it hits.</div> </div> </div> </div>All mentions of the imago in the core book that I found simply mentions the imago as the mental image or construct made out of the mage's thoughts. That said it's also obvious that something mystical going on when forming the imago since it can be detected using AMS (as mentioned earlier in the thread that's how counterspelling works).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:24:17-07:00","id":993247,"title":"","content":"The Imago is the precursor to spellcasting. But as you say, AMS can see it when a Mage begins to cast their spell, suggesting to me that you can feel an impending casting. It makes the whole &quot;Building a ritual to zot someone from across the world&quot; thing much less useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:35:53-07:00","id":993255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=993247#post993247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Imago is the precursor to spellcasting. But as you say, AMS can see it when a Mage begins to cast their spell, suggesting to me that you can feel an impending casting. It makes the whole &quot;Building a ritual to zot someone from across the world&quot; thing much less useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't follow. There's nothing that allows a mage to feel the forming of an imago through one of their sympathetic connections. You need to observe the actual imago in order to become aware of it and being able to counterspell it. Especially the latter since counterspelling is performed by sabotaging the imago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":".  Edited to make it less needlessly antagonistic 10-25-2016, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:38:50-07:00","id":993257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=992889#post992889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You also don't need to use a Reach to turn a spell from ritual casting to instant, since you can cast at your leisure. So some better yantra bonuses than you might get out of tools, and an extra Reach.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> Interesting, for some reason when I was thinking about it 'spirit zoos' came to mind, with ample use of ban dividing everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's no more benefit you get than casting from and secured space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:56:50-07:00","id":993291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=993255#post993255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't follow. There's nothing that allows a mage to feel the forming of an imago through one of their sympathetic connections. You need to observe the actual imago in order to become aware of it and being able to counterspell it. Especially the latter since counterspelling is performed by sabotaging the imago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, so, I went back to take a look here, and found an important point:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2e Core, Page 92</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Active Mage Sight of any Arcanum also reveals all Awakened spells as they are being cast. The mage can see another willworker\u2019s Nimbus flare as he forms the Imago and casts the spell (which, in turn, gives the observant mage a chance to use the Counterspell Attainment if she knows the Arcanum involved).</div> </div> </div> </div>What a Mage is sensing in their Peripheral Sight and seeing in their Active Sight isn't the Imago forming (something that I should've really remembered; the only time you see an Imago is during a Duel Arcane): It's the flaring of the Nimbus of a Mage casting a spell. It also says that the Mage can see it <i>as</i> the Imago is forming, meaning before the spell is actually cast.<br /> <br /> In other words, a Mage's Nimbus flares whenever they start to form an Imago. This is why anyone present can sense it before they cast it. The Awakened aren't suddenly mind-readers (unless they're Mastigoi, the pricks).<br /> <br /> Given how sympathy works, I'd say that the Nimbus would flare around the target too, making sympathetic spells detectable at range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T21:22:41-07:00","id":993306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=993291#post993291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alright, so, I went back to take a look here, and found an important point:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What a Mage is sensing in their Peripheral Sight and seeing in their Active Sight isn't the Imago forming (something that I should've really remembered; the only time you see an Imago is during a Duel Arcane): It's the flaring of the Nimbus of a Mage casting a spell. It also says that the Mage can see it <i>as</i> the Imago is forming, meaning before the spell is actually cast.<br /> <br /> In other words, a Mage's Nimbus flares whenever they start to form an Imago. This is why anyone present can sense it before they cast it. The Awakened aren't suddenly mind-readers (unless they're Mastigoi, the pricks).<br /> <br /> Given how sympathy works, I'd say that the Nimbus would flare around the target too, making sympathetic spells detectable at range.</div> </div> </div> </div>That the subject of a spell would also display the nimbus is beyond the book (and doesn't seem logical to me), but even if that house rule is in place most that I've written still applies. You can still only see it with your active mage sight. And when you see it, what are you going to do about it? You still need to see the caster in order to counterspell.<br /> <br /> Edit: I read the nimbus rules and only the signature nimbus (not the one that flares) are seen on spells and subjects of spells, and only focused mage sight will reveal it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-26-2016, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T22:10:50-07:00","id":993318,"title":"","content":"You might only <i>see</i> the Nimbus with Active Sight but seeing it isn't really the point. Peripheral Sight triggers at the activation of any magical effect. If a Mage's Nimbus radiates around the target of a building spell, that would trigger Peripheral Sight. Given that the book describes a Mage's Nimbus leaving wisps of magic any time they cast a spell, it doesn't seem outlandish to assume this means it builds when the spell does.<br /> <br /> (While I'm at it, it doesn't say a Signature Nimbus can only be detected with Focused Sight; it says that a Mage may recognize any they've seen before using Focused Sight. Big difference.)<br /> <br /> As for what you can do about it... A great deal, really. Raise your magical defenses, for one. Cast Ward on yourself, attempt to weaken or sever the sympathetic thread that binds you to the caster, raise your defenses with Wards and Signs, cast right back at them... The latter in particular is quite important, since it acts as a useful deterrent against being targeted with this sort of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T07:19:54-07:00","id":993483,"title":"","content":"&quot;By the time a spell takes effect and a mage feels it in Peripheral Mage Sight, though, it\u2019s too late to counter; to use this Attainment, the countering mage must see her rival casting in Active Mage Sight.&quot;<br /> <br /> The spell has to take effect before the peripheral mage sight notices it. Hence peripheral mage sight does not notice the spell being built.<br /> <br /> And for what you can do, yes, it's a lot more than I thought about. (In my defense it was way past midnight and I was suffering from insomnia.)<br /> But that is if the ST rules that the subject also exhibits a nimbus during the construction of the imago, which I really don't think it should. The subject isn't part of the spell. It's not even being used and involved in it the way a yantra is. It's the receiver of a spell. It's like sending a mail. You have the pen, the paper, the envelope, the name, the adress and the post stamp as your tools/yantras and they are quite noticably used if you study the process of writing the mail, you see the mail/imago taking form, but the recipient is completely uninvolved until they get the mail. At least that's my take on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-26-2016, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T08:39:06-07:00","id":993515,"title":"","content":"That point about Peripheral not activating prior to the spell being cast is a good one. That would seem to suggest that, even if a Nimbus does surround the spell's target, no-one notices until it's too late.<br /> <br /> It also says something interesting about the Nimbus in general, really.<br /> <br /> I'd say you're right, that RAW Peripheral Sight isn't pinged by a spell building up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T01:32:14-07:00","id":995549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=992845#post992845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A decent amount less now that &quot;remote viewing&quot; is a distinct range modifier with no Arcanum requirement, I'd think.</div> </div> </div> </div>(My email notifications stopped working - I thought this thread had died on 24th...)<br /> Can you direct me to the area in the book where this is spelled out? I was only aware that it applied to familiars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 10-30-2016, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T03:31:52-07:00","id":995570,"title":"","content":"Remote viewing in real time is considered a form of sensory range, requiring nothing but an extra reach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Advanced Range factor is sensory, meaning that the<br /> mage must be able to directly see, hear, or sense her subject. Viewing<br /> a subject remotely but in real-time, whether by security camera or<br /> magic scrying window, requires an additional Reach. </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile the space 2 enabled sympathetic reach is a separate thing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the mage has the Space Attainment<br /> Sympathetic Range or the Time Attainment Temporal Sympathy,<br /> she can cast spells without the need to sense her subject. </div> </div> </div>The familiar ability is simply a consequence of the shared senses. You're just using them as a camera, basically.<br /> <br /> This is all on the range explanation on page 113-114.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T07:00:37-07:00","id":995611,"title":"","content":"The comparison of the two mechanics boils down so that if you cast via Remote Viewing you spend two Reach, one for Sensory Range and then one for casting through your remote viewing focus of choice (Familiar, live feed, etc), and if you cast Sympathetically you have a Sympathetic connection, a Sympathetic Yantra, spend a Reach for Sensory Range and spend a mana to activate the Sympathetic attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:32:26-07:00","id":995718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=995570#post995570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remote viewing in real time is considered a form of sensory range, requiring nothing but an extra reach.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile the space 2 enabled sympathetic reach is a separate thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> The familiar ability is simply a consequence of the shared senses. You're just using them as a camera, basically.<br /> <br /> This is all on the range explanation on page 113-114.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks - that clears up some confusion on my part. I actually conflated Remote Viewing with Scrying, so I originally thought you meant you could spy on things from a distance magically without space. When discussing casting, I never considered remote viewing could just mean watching live TV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:41:26-07:00","id":995722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=995611#post995611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The comparison of the two mechanics boils down so that if you cast via Remote Viewing you spend two Reach, one for Sensory Range and then one for casting through your remote viewing focus of choice (Familiar, live feed, etc), and if you cast Sympathetically you have a Sympathetic connection, a Sympathetic Yantra, spend a Reach for Sensory Range and spend a mana to activate the Sympathetic attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. After a few of the responses on this thread, I may be able to dial back the &quot;space 2&quot; craziness that grinds my gears in our games. I really think from what I guess can be called &quot;Awakening Aesthetics&quot; that no mage should ever select an Arcana with the goal of gaining one or two options. Each Arcana is a whole school of thought / point of view that the mage is embracing. Gaining space just for scrying and sympathetic range felt like gaining a masters in computer science just for the purpose of being better at modding PC games for your personal enjoyment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:09:13-07:00","id":995846,"title":"","content":"Mages do stuff for practical purposes all the time. You'd probably get more mileage out of showing the limitations of relying just on Sympathetic casting, and providing creative instances of Space in use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T21:29:30-07:00","id":995951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=993135#post993135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or with Space magic at all. Since it mentions locking a Space into place though I'm not entirely sure it's mobile. Maybe with a Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Reach required; The wording in the spell Ward includes &quot;Cast on an area or individual subjects&quot;, in case you don't feel like looking it up.<br /> <br /> (Must say, the electronic indeces in the new book are <i>way</i> nicer than the older stuff. Man.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:38:07-07:00","id":997127,"title":"","content":"For casting at range, in this day and age, you can just as easily use Forces. Sit at your computer, wave your hand and let the magic find the IP of the person you're targeting. Now, wiggle your fingers to turn their webcam or their phone cameras on and now you're seeing them in live-feed. Now, chant a few words in High Speech, Reach a bit, and you can fry them by redirecting the flow of electricity in their houses to their bodies while laughing maniacally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:20:09-07:00","id":997148,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't turning their camera on require sympathetic casting? It's not in sensory range and you're not remotely viewing it.<br /> Or maybe you cast on your own computer to hack the camera. I have no idea how spells interact with computers and the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:22:19-07:00","id":997149,"title":"","content":"I think you're possibly stretching what counts as remote viewing a little bit in the middle there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:28:26-07:00","id":997153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=997148#post997148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't turning their camera on require sympathetic casting? It's not in sensory range and you're not remotely viewing it.<br /> Or maybe you cast on your own computer to hack the camera. I have no idea how spells interact with computers and the internet.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use Fate (Lucky Number, Fate 2, Core 136) to correctly guess any password; given that that that spell will also let you correctly guess a phone number, it seems plausible to me that it would let you correctly guess an IP address. I'm not seeing any Forces spell applicable to penetrating computer security, but I may be missing something.<br /> <br /> So if they're online, and their device of choice has a webcam that can be accessed remotely by some sort of password-protected means, then you can turn it on and use it to see them, and go from there. If any of those steps is missing, however, or if they're just not in the webcam's field of view, you are out of luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:34:20-07:00","id":997155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=997153#post997153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can use Fate (Lucky Number, Fate 2, Core 136) to correctly guess any password; given that that that spell will also let you correctly guess a phone number, it seems plausible to me that it would let you correctly guess an IP address. I'm not seeing any Forces spell applicable to penetrating computer security, but I may be missing something.<br /> <br /> So if they're online, and their device of choice has a webcam that can be accessed remotely by some sort of password-protected means, then you can turn it on and use it to see them, and go from there. If any of those steps is missing, however, or if they're just not in the webcam's field of view, you are out of luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, Forces is to computers as Mind is to people. All the data and connectivity is maintained by electricity after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:48:04-07:00","id":997166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=997155#post997155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, Forces is to computers as Mind is to people. All the data and connectivity is maintained by electricity after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if one accepts that equivalency*, that doesn't grant the power to use it outside sensory range without a sympathetic link or pre-existing remote viewing. You can certainly use it to manipulate the signals being sent from your computer, but you have no access to the computer at the other end of the connection.<br /> <br /> *Which seems questionable to me; I don't see anything in the book suggesting that Forces grants the same level of access and fine control over this one small part of its purview that Mind does to the <i>only</i> thing in its purview. But I am open to being proven wrong if I've overlooked something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:50:47-07:00","id":997169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=997166#post997166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can certainly use it to manipulate the signals being sent from your computer, but you have no access to the computer at the other end of the connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's where your dots in Computer come in. Not everything needs to be done by magic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:03:37-07:00","id":997179,"title":"","content":"Right, but you can also use your dots in Computer by... using your computer. Why use Forces when you have at your disposal a device purpose-built for sending and receiving digital signals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:16:37-07:00","id":997189,"title":"","content":"Well, sitting in your demesne with Mind 2 and a single dot of Computer and you can basically turn yourself into Hackerman from Kung Fury (Add Time 2: You can now hack time). Only need enough yantras to get your Potency up and then you're able to hack just about anything that can be hacked remotely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:40:37-07:00","id":997205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=997179#post997179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but you can also use your dots in Computer by... using your computer. Why use Forces when you have at your disposal a device purpose-built for sending and receiving digital signals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces allows you to skip the middle <s>man</s> device.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:07:33-07:00","id":997217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=997166#post997166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which seems questionable to me; I don't see anything in the book suggesting that Forces grants the same level of access and fine control over this one small part of its purview that Mind does to the <i>only</i> thing in its purview. But I am open to being proven wrong if I've overlooked something.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lack of spells for it in the book doesn't mean it can't be done. 1e got an update, but ideas in it, including programs falling under the purview of Forces aren't necessarily negated simply by their lack of being mentioned.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the equivalency doesn't hold up completely. Computers aren't capable of being independent agents with supernatural powers for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:28:33-07:00","id":997223,"title":"","content":"Well, you could potentially manage something like that with Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:34:09-07:00","id":997228,"title":"","content":"The Cray does that. You could attach Mind to it and, without having spirit, have it just be a sapient computer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:12:54-07:00","id":997252,"title":"","content":"Yes, obviously, those are both options. I only constructed that post in order to address the concern expressed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12425\" data-vbnamecard=\"12425\">General Tacticus</a> after I made a comparison between Forces and programs and Mind and minds to show that the comparison was being taken too literally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T23:19:11-07:00","id":998629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=997217#post997217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The lack of spells for it in the book doesn't mean it can't be done. 1e got an update, but ideas in it, including programs falling under the purview of Forces aren't necessarily negated simply by their lack of being mentioned.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the equivalency doesn't hold up completely. Computers aren't capable of being independent agents with supernatural powers for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absence of evidence isn't conclusive evidence of absence, true (although it is suggestive), but it's not evidence of <i>presence</i> either. What grounds are there to attribute a Mind Arcanum-level of fine control over computers to Forces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T06:13:58-07:00","id":998717,"title":"","content":"i direct you to the Forces section of the Free Council book.<br /> <br /> Also, because programs are a physical phenomena mainly operating on controlled electrical currents and that's the purview of Forces. You're not stuck using just Forces to manipulate them, but it's the most direct route of intervention. I'd say it's a fairly brute force approach though since it won't leave Lasting effects on altered or generated programs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 11-05-2016, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:02:52-07:00","id":998894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=998629#post998629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absence of evidence isn't conclusive evidence of absence, true (although it is suggestive), but it's not evidence of <i>presence</i> either. What grounds are there to attribute a Mind Arcanum-level of fine control over computers to Forces?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dave has previously discussed how Forces generally controlled computers and electronic equipment, including matters like hacking and the internet, with Matter have some purview over physical media like a disks or thumb drives. It's unclear in 2e whether Mind would be necessary for decryption and similar matters. Hopefully, this issues will be discussed in detail in Dave's Mage FAQ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T02:55:51-08:00","id":999639,"title":"","content":"Back to topic: While Space 2 is for sure useful, I would like to point out, that you actually lose a lot if you go for it. Scrying is probably a must have in a group, but depending on group size, one or two Mages with it should be enough. It's not explicitely stated, but I would let you include additional percievers of the scrying window with a reach or increased spell factors.<br /> For casting trough sympathatic connections you need to remind yourself, that this isn't so easy (withstand, yantra, having a sympathetic connection). For at least the sympathetic connection to the target you have to get in close to the target at least once or do some really good reasearch. With only Space 2 you got little option for increasing your chances of sympathetic spells through strengthening connections and forth.<br /> In comparison, you could use the same amout of experience to get your primary arcanums 4th and 5th dot (at storytells discression of course), which adds immensly more powerful options to your arsenal and just ask somebody else in the group to give you a scrying window of your subject and cast via remote casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T04:39:11-08:00","id":999667,"title":"","content":"I think your end of the scrying window is just visible to everyone naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:49:35-08:00","id":999689,"title":"","content":"That would make it even easier to have a single Space 4 Mage doing the scrying for the group than having everybody have to do it themself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:32:42-08:00","id":1001492,"title":"","content":"I'm having a bit of a hard time understanding the mechanics of scrying and sympathetic range. If a mage with Gnosis 2, Space 3 mage that has a item with medium sympathetic strength (a letter written by the subject) and wants to scry them, then is this how things would work?<br /> <br /> Starting dice pool of 5. Yantras are the item with sympathy (the letter) and a High Speech mantra. The item gives no bonus, the High Speech gives +2 dice. The mage uses two reach: one for fast spell casting and one for advanced duration. This doesn't go over her free limit of 2 reach for this practice. The sympathetic withstand is 2, so the potency must be 3 for the spell to do anything, so the mage takes a dice penalty of -4 to increase the potency by 2. The final dice pool is 3 (5+2-4), and if successful, the mage can view the subject for a scene.<br /> <br /> Am I missing anything? Do you need to use the reach for sensory casting for this spell? Do you need to pay one Mana as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11211-space-butler","name":"Space Butler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:37:32-08:00","id":1001496,"title":"","content":"Yes, you're hypothetical Mage doesn't have a personal Sympathetic connection to his target. He could use Borrow Threads from his Sympathetic object though I'd rule that makes that object defunct as a Sympathetic Yantra, not sure about others.<br /> <br /> You're also forgetting the automatic Primary Factors given by arcana.<br /> <br /> Yes, you need Reach on Sensory Range and to pay a mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 11-10-2016, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:18:49-08:00","id":1001520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Space Butler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=1001492#post1001492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having a bit of a hard time understanding the mechanics of scrying and sympathetic range. If a mage with Gnosis 2, Space 3 mage that has a item with medium sympathetic strength (a letter written by the subject) and wants to scry them, then is this how things would work?<br /> <br /> Starting dice pool of 5. Yantras are the item with sympathy (the letter) and a High Speech mantra. The item gives no bonus, the High Speech gives +2 dice. The mage uses two reach: one for fast spell casting and one for advanced duration. This doesn't go over her free limit of 2 reach for this practice. The sympathetic withstand is 2, so the potency must be 3 for the spell to do anything, so the mage takes a dice penalty of -4 to increase the potency by 2. The final dice pool is 3 (5+2-4), and if successful, the mage can view the subject for a scene.<br /> <br /> Am I missing anything? Do you need to use the reach for sensory casting for this spell? Do you need to pay one Mana as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mage has to have a sympathetic connection to the subject. Just having an object with a sympathetic connection is not enough. Luckily Borrow Threads can help with that.<br /> <br /> Borrow Threads (Space \u2022\u2022)<br /> Two free Reaches for Instant Casting and Advanced Duration.<br /> Withstand is 2 so Potency will be increased by two steps for a -4 dice penalty.<br /> High Speech is used as a Yantra for +2 dice.<br /> 5+2-4 = 3 dice<br /> <br /> If successful the Mage now has the same sympathy for up to a week but will probably just cancel Borrow Threads when done scrying.<br /> <br /> Scry (Space \u2022\u2022)<br /> Two free Reaches for Instant Casting and Advanced Duration. One additional Reach will have to be spent for Sensory Range as it's a prerequisite for using Sympathetic Range.<br /> Withstand is 3 (2 from the Medium Connection plus 1 if the Sympathetic Name isn't used as a Yantra) so Potency will be increased by three steps for a -6 dice penalty.<br /> High Speech is used as a Yantra for +2 dice. A depiction of the subject is used as a sympathetic Yantra. (The letter has a sympathetic connection, but it isn't a representation of the subject so it can't be used as a sympathetic Yantra.)<br /> 1 Mana is spent for Sympathetic Range.<br /> 5+2-6 = 1 die<br /> 1 Paradox die from the extra Reach<br /> <br /> Sympathetic casting is quite useful, but it's difficult to really utilize until Gnosis 3 when you can use an additional Yantra. You also want spells you often cast sympathetically as Rotes so you get more Reaches and Mudra as a Yantra. (Mastigos are blessed in that they get both Space and Mind since it's possible to boost skills with Mind 3 meaning they have an easier time getting +5 from Mudras.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:57:28-08:00","id":1001531,"title":"","content":"Thank you. So can the Sympathy Yantra used for the scry spell be a symbolic sympathy i.e. just the subject's name or a drawing of the subject?<br /> <br /> If she were to cast the scry spell with advanced duration (and have the spell last a week), can she end the Borrow Threads spell without affecting the Scry spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11211-space-butler","name":"Space Butler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T16:14:47-08:00","id":1001537,"title":"","content":"Material, representional and symbolic sympathetic yantras are all possible options when casting sympathetically. This includes physical parts of the subject as well as drawings. Page 122 has a list.<br /> <br /> My first reaction was that Scry would be cancelled, but I don't think so. Sensory range spells don't end just because the subject leaves sensory range so sympathetically cast spells shouldn't either. The spell exists independently of what connection the mage has to the subject. Also, since the subject is subject to the mage's spell, the mage gains a Weak sympathetic connection to the subject anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T23:43:36-08:00","id":1001648,"title":"","content":"Also note: the letter itself would never count as a sympathetic yantra, no matter its connection to the subject. The sympathetic yantra needs to represent the subject you are casting on. It therefore needs some kind of symbolism of the subject. If you find a hair or some skin cells of the subject on the letter, that would be able to be a sympathetic yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T00:46:25-08:00","id":1001662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991833-space-2-does-anyone-do-without-it?p=1001648#post1001648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also note: the letter itself would never count as a sympathetic yantra, no matter its connection to the subject. The sympathetic yantra needs to represent the subject you are casting on. It therefore needs some kind of symbolism of the subject. If you find a hair or some skin cells of the subject on the letter, that would be able to be a sympathetic yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just write their sympathetic name on a piece of paper.<br /> Or make a drawing of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T02:55:52-08:00","id":1001700,"title":"","content":"Voodoo dolls seem an obvious example of a low-tier Sympathy yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T08:23:31-08:00","id":1001766,"title":"","content":"We had our first session last week and I thought it was funny how some yantra sort of cover everything for some arcana. Like with Time, you could use a watch or hourglass for most, though I don't think all, of the spells. With Matter, you would need considerably more to do the wide variety of specific effects. A carbon cube wouldn't be as useful as Time's clock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:11:01-08:00","id":1002044,"title":"","content":"That's because Time is a surprisingly narrow focus. Time only does one thing: Be Time. It is a broad purview in effect, but ultimately the only thing Time manipulates is one thing that only really exists in one form anywhere and everywhere. Matter, meanwhile, is diverse. Varied. Matter might all be atoms, but those atoms form into gases, liquids, solids; Matter can be crystals, metals, loose soil, floaty air, boiling magma, flowing water, and so much more.<br /> <br /> Time is, in a sense, remarkably one-note; it's just so big of a note that it's hard to notice. Matter is a symphony and it's hard to play a symphony with one instrument, y'know?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T12:40:04-08:00","id":1009895,"title":"","content":"I haven't started my 2e game yet, but my 1e game ran for 50 sessions and the Obrimos didn't bother getting Space. The Thyrsus only acquired it in our 40th session or so. The other two characters (Mastigos and Acanthus) made pretty good use of it for the whole chronicle.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's strictly necessary and I would think long and hard if I were a player about getting Space 2 instead of becoming a Master in one of my ruling Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}